No way, no way, it fell in already.

72
00:05:09,019 --> 00:05:12,759
Oh, what a terrific sound that was.

73
00:05:12,839 --> 00:05:14,619
She doesn't have to panic that much.

74
00:05:14,839 --> 00:05:16,359
Anyway, we're going on ahead.

75
00:05:16,559 --> 00:05:16,939
Okay.

76
00:05:16,939 --> 00:05:20,499
It really does feel like I'm still just Duck.

77
00:05:20,599 --> 00:05:21,819
Nothing's changed at all.

78
00:05:24,219 --> 00:05:24,819
Roo.

79
00:05:25,819 --> 00:05:27,239
She'll come back, right?

80
00:05:28,199 --> 00:05:29,659
Roo is Roo, right?

81
00:05:29,999 --> 00:05:32,519
She's definitely not Princess Krayhi, right?

82
00:05:34,039 --> 00:05:35,339
Good morning, Duck.

83
00:05:37,079 --> 00:05:39,039
Good morning, Mito.

84
00:05:39,039 --> 00:05:41,459
Oh, look here.

85
00:05:41,459 --> 00:05:44,259
Is your wound healed yet?

86
00:05:46,499 --> 00:05:51,139
It had started to improve, but seeing your face again has triggered fresh stabs of pain.

87
00:05:51,919 --> 00:05:55,539
She was worried because you were absent from school for a week, Fakir.

88
00:05:55,539 --> 00:05:58,259
It isn't kind of you to talk that way.

89
00:05:59,159 --> 00:06:00,739
Please don't mind him, Duck.

90
00:06:01,219 --> 00:06:03,059
Will you at least stay friendly with me?

91
00:06:03,459 --> 00:06:06,619
You're the only friend whom I can tell everything.

92
00:06:07,759 --> 00:06:08,279
Sure.

93
00:06:09,339 --> 00:06:10,559
Tell everything.

94
00:06:11,299 --> 00:06:14,319
I'm hiding the fact that I'm Princess Tutu from Mito.

95
00:06:14,959 --> 00:06:16,759
And the fact that I'm a duck, too.

96
00:06:17,599 --> 00:06:19,199
Am I being unfair?

97
00:06:19,779 --> 00:06:21,619
I have to tell him, don't I?

98
00:06:22,239 --> 00:06:22,539
But...

99
00:06:23,159 --> 00:06:23,939
Are you all right?

100
00:06:23,939 --> 00:06:25,859
Um, I...

101
00:06:25,859 --> 00:06:27,719
Well, the truth is...

102
00:06:27,719 --> 00:06:28,719
The truth is...

103
00:06:28,719 --> 00:06:29,799
Princess Tutu!

104
00:06:30,039 --> 00:06:30,439
What?

105
00:06:30,799 --> 00:06:32,339
I see her flying.

106
00:06:33,079 --> 00:06:34,859
Hold on, maybe it's a crocodile.

107
00:06:35,199 --> 00:06:35,899
What do you think?

108
00:06:36,219 --> 00:06:36,659
What?

109
00:06:36,879 --> 00:06:37,799
There's nothing there.

110
00:06:38,459 --> 00:06:41,059
Princess Tutu and a crocodile are totally different.

111
00:06:41,979 --> 00:06:42,859
Um, Fakir?

112
00:06:43,199 --> 00:06:44,239
You're so right.

113
00:06:44,499 --> 00:06:45,899
I probably just imagined it.

114
00:06:46,439 --> 00:06:48,359
Though I could have sworn I saw a flying cow.

115
00:06:48,859 --> 00:06:49,379
Cow?

116
00:06:49,879 --> 00:06:50,519
It's nothing.

117
00:06:50,979 --> 00:06:51,599
Never mind.

118
00:06:51,599 --> 00:06:53,019
You're not making sense.

119
00:06:53,939 --> 00:06:54,459
That's hot.

120
00:06:54,699 --> 00:06:55,279
Where's Duck?

121
00:06:55,399 --> 00:06:55,959
Who knows?

122
00:06:56,479 --> 00:06:59,459
It's likely my comments put her off, so she went on ahead.

123
00:06:59,819 --> 00:07:00,139
Yeah.

124
00:07:01,359 --> 00:07:03,999
You need to treat girls more nicely, Fakir.

125
00:07:05,999 --> 00:07:08,899
Say, Mito, what do you think of Princess Tutu?

126
00:07:09,359 --> 00:07:10,439
That's rather sudden.

127
00:07:10,439 --> 00:07:13,939
Um, she always disappears after she returns a piece of your heart.

128
00:07:14,559 --> 00:07:16,459
Don't you want to know who she is?

129
00:07:16,939 --> 00:07:17,719
Sure I do.

130
00:07:18,059 --> 00:07:18,339
Uh.

131
00:07:18,859 --> 00:07:21,999
But maybe right now, it's best for me not to know.

132
00:07:22,579 --> 00:07:26,199
Because I'm certain there will come a day when she will be ready to tell me.

133
00:07:26,199 --> 00:07:32,479
Right now, I'm thinking more about how I have to get all of my feelings back as soon as I can.

134
00:07:33,139 --> 00:07:35,299
With help from Princess Tutu.

135
00:07:36,259 --> 00:07:36,659
Muto.

136
00:07:37,059 --> 00:07:39,019
You'll help me too, won't you, Fakir?

137
00:07:39,139 --> 00:07:40,959
Well, I am supposed to be a knight.

138
00:07:41,659 --> 00:07:44,059
I knew I could count on you to help me, Fakir.

139
00:07:44,059 --> 00:07:49,559
And when that's finished, I'll go back into the story.

140
00:07:50,219 --> 00:07:50,659
Muto.

141
00:07:51,419 --> 00:07:53,359
Is that truly what you want, Muto?

142
00:07:53,739 --> 00:07:56,279
As the story's prince, I belong there.

143
00:07:57,379 --> 00:07:58,419
I see that.

144
00:08:00,679 --> 00:08:01,479
Shall we go?

145
00:08:02,039 --> 00:08:03,879
Mr. Cat will be angry at us if we're late.

146
00:08:05,019 --> 00:08:06,879
You give me a lot of trouble.

147
00:08:07,119 --> 00:08:07,559
Fak!

148
00:08:07,679 --> 00:08:08,839
What are you talking about?

149
00:08:08,859 --> 00:08:09,939
It's your fault!

150
00:08:10,119 --> 00:08:12,899
You can just be late and have Mr. Cat get mad at you!

151
00:08:12,899 --> 00:08:14,279
Oh, oh, but wait.

152
00:08:14,759 --> 00:08:18,319
Maybe Fakir did that on purpose to let me hear what Muto just said.

153
00:08:18,839 --> 00:08:20,579
Oh no, I'm going to be late too!

154
00:08:42,899 --> 00:08:46,899
Looks like Mr. Cat's pretty freaking angry.

155
00:08:47,259 --> 00:08:48,019
This is great!

156
00:08:48,259 --> 00:08:49,539
I hope Duck comes soon.

157
00:08:49,939 --> 00:08:51,159
That would be perfect.

158
00:09:00,159 --> 00:09:00,519
Softly...

159
00:09:00,519 --> 00:09:02,839
Miss Duck, I presume?

160
00:09:03,299 --> 00:09:03,839
Yes, sir!

161
00:09:03,839 --> 00:09:08,899
I left the dorm at the normal time, but on my way I saw a crocodile and a cow flying in the sky and...

162
00:09:08,899 --> 00:09:12,799
Miss Duck, as usual, I see you act like you own the place.

163
00:09:13,059 --> 00:09:16,439
I have to say, you're exactly like the students in the advanced class.

164
00:09:16,599 --> 00:09:17,699
Oh, no, sir.

165
00:09:17,739 --> 00:09:19,039
I don't think I'm that great.

166
00:09:19,279 --> 00:09:26,339
If you insist on coming to my class late, I'll either drop you to the probationary class again,

167
00:09:26,339 --> 00:09:30,539
or, or, or have you marry me!

168
00:09:32,079 --> 00:09:32,799
See that?

169
00:09:32,939 --> 00:09:33,939
Look how hard she's trying!

170
00:09:34,039 --> 00:09:34,859
Please forgive her!

171
00:09:35,439 --> 00:09:38,399
Probation is one thing, but please don't make her marry you!

172
00:09:42,399 --> 00:09:42,999
Muto...

173
00:09:42,999 --> 00:09:47,239
I'm glad I got to hear what he had to say.

174
00:09:47,679 --> 00:09:51,959
I'm going to have to try even harder until I get back all the pieces of Muto's heart.

175
00:09:52,399 --> 00:09:53,339
That's right, Duck!

176
00:09:53,339 --> 00:09:55,599
I don't know what you're talking about, but you've got to try!

177
00:09:55,899 --> 00:09:58,959
Try your best and hardest and fail spectacularly, okay?

178
00:10:01,739 --> 00:10:04,099
What calm days these are!

179
00:10:04,239 --> 00:10:06,519
What blissful, peaceful days!

180
00:10:06,779 --> 00:10:09,039
But they won't continue forever, you know?

181
00:10:09,239 --> 00:10:11,879
That's what's so great about Stormy's.

182
00:10:11,879 --> 00:10:28,439
Listen up, everyone!

183
00:10:29,239 --> 00:10:33,719
In ballet, the most important thing is to practice second most practice.

184
00:10:34,359 --> 00:10:37,199
Third, fourth, and fifth most are also practice.

185
00:10:37,739 --> 00:10:39,859
Why exactly do we practice, then?

186
00:10:39,859 --> 00:10:42,699
We do it to master the basics.

187
00:10:43,979 --> 00:10:45,879
Today, I share a story with you.

188
00:10:46,279 --> 00:10:47,979
Please listen carefully,

189
00:10:48,679 --> 00:10:51,559
without letting your eyes wander.

190
00:10:51,839 --> 00:10:52,199
Yes!

191
00:10:52,619 --> 00:10:53,559
You got it, sir!

192
00:10:54,159 --> 00:10:58,439
Yes, this was back when I was a young student attending ballet school.

193
00:10:58,439 --> 00:11:04,259
I happened to get the rare chance to observe Mr. Meowzynski practicing.

194
00:11:04,799 --> 00:11:06,359
Meowzynski?

195
00:11:06,719 --> 00:11:08,379
The legendary ballet dancer.

196
00:11:08,459 --> 00:11:10,039
Poor, clueless little duck.

197
00:11:10,539 --> 00:11:17,339
We ballet school students were helping out with the backstage preparations for a performance of Mr. Meowzynski's.

198
00:11:17,339 --> 00:11:20,359
I was still only a year and three months old.

199
00:11:20,359 --> 00:11:21,799
A cheeky young boy.

200
00:11:25,799 --> 00:11:26,759
Oh, no, no.

201
00:11:26,759 --> 00:11:47,999
Yes, it was Mr. Meowzynski himself, the man renowned as a genius for his novel choreography and the gravity-defying jumps, which people call miraculous.

202
00:11:47,999 --> 00:12:01,459
But that day, all Mr. Meowzynski was doing was just slowly, very slowly, practicing the basics over and over and over and over.

203
00:12:01,459 --> 00:12:30,879
Before I knew it, I found myself asking him questions.

204
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:37,359
I thought a dancer as famous as you would have a more special practice routine, I said.

205
00:12:37,719 --> 00:12:39,259
This is how he answered me.

206
00:12:39,599 --> 00:12:46,859
Someone who has not mastered basics cannot achieve advanced techniques or cultivates a noble spirit.

207
00:12:47,939 --> 00:12:53,519
These shoes were given to me that day by Mr. Meowzynski after our conversation.

208
00:12:53,779 --> 00:12:59,959
And having received them, I swore upon these shoes to dedicate the rest of my life to ballet.

209
00:12:59,959 --> 00:13:03,559
In other words, he's just saying, practice the basics diligently.

210
00:13:04,059 --> 00:13:10,299
But I think some people will never get good no matter how hard or often they practice the basics, so you can't let it get to you.

211
00:13:10,959 --> 00:13:17,459
These shoes have suffered a lot of wear and tear, but to me, they are the most beautiful shoes in the world.

212
00:13:17,459 --> 00:13:23,399
Oh, what's wrong with Mewtwo?

213
00:13:25,399 --> 00:13:27,139
What was that?

214
00:13:27,139 --> 00:13:39,159
Mewtwo!

215
00:13:39,159 --> 00:13:41,779
Mewtwo, you came back here?

216
00:13:41,779 --> 00:14:01,539
Mewtwo, you just disappeared from class all of a sudden. Where did you go? I couldn't find you.

217
00:14:01,539 --> 00:14:05,799
I wonder what happened. I started to feel sick, and after that...

218
00:14:05,799 --> 00:14:10,799
Your desire for immediate restoration won't hasten things. Don't try too hard.

219
00:14:11,639 --> 00:14:13,919
So I can become like you, Fakir?

220
00:14:14,379 --> 00:14:15,139
What did you say?

221
00:14:15,959 --> 00:14:17,299
That's not possible.

222
00:14:19,099 --> 00:14:23,219
Say, Fakir, I have something to tell you. Will you listen?

223
00:14:23,219 --> 00:14:30,139
I trust you firmly engraved Mr. Mewzinski's words in your minds.

224
00:14:30,299 --> 00:14:35,519
Even if they diligently practice the basics, people who aren't going to get good will never get good.

225
00:14:35,859 --> 00:14:37,179
Wait, how did it go?

226
00:14:38,699 --> 00:14:40,939
Anyway, be on time for class tomorrow.

227
00:14:41,559 --> 00:14:43,459
Yes, sir. But I doubt I can't.

228
00:14:43,479 --> 00:14:45,659
Well, no need to let it get to you too much.

229
00:14:45,799 --> 00:14:48,859
That's right, Deb. Being late isn't a central part of your charm.

230
00:14:48,859 --> 00:14:56,419
What was that scream? Mr. Cat? Could it be an incident?

231
00:14:58,479 --> 00:15:01,739
Oh my, that duck doesn't even disguise her curiosity.

232
00:15:01,819 --> 00:15:02,939
That was your fault.

233
00:15:03,059 --> 00:15:03,419
What?

234
00:15:08,079 --> 00:15:11,099
And where are you going, duck?

235
00:15:12,699 --> 00:15:13,759
Mr. Cat!

236
00:15:13,919 --> 00:15:17,819
Oh dear, dear, dear. It's duck's fault. This is duck's fault, isn't it?

237
00:15:17,819 --> 00:15:25,039
There are Mewzinski's shoes.

238
00:15:25,079 --> 00:15:25,959
How awful.

239
00:15:26,199 --> 00:15:27,899
Did Mr. Cat do it himself?

240
00:15:29,739 --> 00:15:33,119
Why can't I get Mewto off my mind? Why?

241
00:15:34,379 --> 00:15:35,819
Duck, where are you going?

242
00:15:39,919 --> 00:15:41,599
How did it go? Did you find Mewto?

243
00:15:41,699 --> 00:15:42,379
Didn't find him.

244
00:15:42,439 --> 00:15:43,039
Not anywhere.

245
00:15:43,039 --> 00:15:43,839
Nowhere.

246
00:15:44,499 --> 00:15:45,459
Not a trace.

247
00:15:46,839 --> 00:15:47,799
I see then.

248
00:15:47,939 --> 00:15:49,339
Hey, is something going on with him?

249
00:15:49,459 --> 00:15:50,219
With Fakir.

250
00:15:50,299 --> 00:15:51,059
He's acting weird.

251
00:15:51,099 --> 00:15:52,199
Yeah, really weird.

252
00:15:52,919 --> 00:15:54,179
He's up in the library.

253
00:15:54,379 --> 00:15:55,339
Hold up in there.

254
00:15:55,419 --> 00:15:56,219
Research, maybe.

255
00:15:56,479 --> 00:15:57,619
Sure seems like it.

256
00:15:57,839 --> 00:15:58,679
How on Fakir?

257
00:15:58,779 --> 00:15:59,179
Library?

258
00:15:59,739 --> 00:16:00,259
Uh-oh.

259
00:16:00,479 --> 00:16:01,259
Forget what we said.

260
00:16:01,399 --> 00:16:02,679
You didn't hear it from us.

261
00:16:02,679 --> 00:16:04,759
It's not like we're into being nosy.

262
00:16:04,959 --> 00:16:05,859
Except we are.

263
00:16:06,179 --> 00:16:06,359
Ah!

264
00:16:10,359 --> 00:16:12,979
Library? What's Fakir doing in there?

265
00:16:13,779 --> 00:16:16,159
It's more important to find Mewto now.

266
00:16:17,019 --> 00:16:17,319
Oh.

267
00:16:19,019 --> 00:16:20,199
Is he there?

268
00:16:21,659 --> 00:16:22,739
Can't see.

